THIRD-PARTY DERIVATIVE WORK - ORE INTERMEDIATES AND PLATINUM COIL

The missing ore intermediates listed in ore_materials.json use recoloured
Mekanism dust, dirty dust, clump, shard, crystal and slurry templates from
10.7.19.85. The MIT notice and permission reproduced above apply to these
derivatives. Specs and most new metal Gems derive from Oritech 1.2.7's Small
Clumps and Gems, by Rearth, under CC0-1.0. Titanium and Corronium Gem silhouettes
and facets are individually drawn. Existing native Gems are not replaced.

Dense Charges are original circular dust-pile drawings. Activated Crystals use
the Mekanism crystal silhouette with a modified pulse. Their material palettes
follow the corresponding native processing forms or ingots. The source asset
mapping and hashes are recorded alongside the integrated files in ore_materials.json.

Raw Voiderite, Raw Bloody and Raw Ostrum recolour Mojang's raw_iron.png under the
same game-modification terms as Raw Eezo. Ostrum Ingot recolours AnvilCraft's
titanium_ingot.png, by Gugle and XeKr, under LGPL-3.0, as described above for Eezo.

  assets/bertieprogression/textures/item/platinum_coil.png

derives from the same CC0 Oritech Magnetic Coil source as Electric Coil. Its
windings follow Oritech Platinum and its exposed top core follows the Malum
Malignant Pewter palette, preserving the coil's shade regions and geometry.

MATERIAL FORM PALETTES

Bronze Sheet samples Mekanism's ingot_bronze.png palette, by Aidan C. Brady,
under the MIT permission reproduced above. Platinum Rod and Wire sample
Oritech's platinum_ingot.png palette under CC0-1.0, retaining the original
material-form geometries. Dense Coal Charge is an original drawing using
Mekanism Coal Dust colors. Integrated source paths and hashes are recorded
in refining_assets.json.

Every other asset here is original.


